From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:25:09 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] RenderManager: release at the nearest vsync without clock
 sync

When the display rate is not a multiple of the frame rate, clock sync is
off and a picture is released at the first vsync at or after its time.
It reaches the screen half a display period late on average, about 8 ms
at 60 Hz, while the audio follows the clock.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/RenderManager.cpp
@@ -0,6 +0,9 @@
   else
   {
     m_dvdClock.SetVsyncAdjust(0);
+    // with no lock to the display, release at the nearest vsync
+    if (!isPaused)
+      renderPts += frametime / 2;
   }
 
   CLog::LogFC(LOGDEBUG, LOGAVTIMING,
